 # Support bundle redaction
 
-Existing action root_kind is exposed through api.dispatch and python cli.py, accepting one JSON object on stdin and writing one JSON result.
+Actions are exposed through `api.dispatch` and `python cli.py`, accepting one JSON object on stdin and writing one JSON result to stdout.
+
+## Actions
+
+### root_kind
+
+Returns `"object"`, `"array"`, or `"scalar"` for `payload["document"]`.
+
+### redact
+
+Input fields:
+
+- `document`: any JSON value (null, booleans, integers, strings, arrays, string-keyed objects), nesting depth at most 10 and at most 500 values total; no floats.
+- `keys`: list of at most 50 strings.
+- `replacement`: a scalar JSON value (null, boolean, integer with magnitude at most 10**12, or string).
+
+Returns a deep copy of `document` in which every object member whose key matches a listed key case-insensitively (Python `str.casefold()`, no whitespace stripping) has its entire value replaced by `replacement`. Replacement happens at any depth; the replaced value is not traversed further. Arrays are traversed, scalars stay unchanged, object keys and array order are preserved, and untouched values keep exact types (booleans are not integers). Input objects are never mutated and no returned mutable container aliases an input container.
+
+Example invocation:
+
+```
+echo '{"action":"redact","document":{"Secret":{"a":[1,true]},"keep":{"secret":99}},"keys":["secret"],"replacement":null}' | python cli.py
+```
+
+prints `{"Secret": null, "keep": {"secret": null}}`.
+
+## Boundaries and errors
+
+Depth 10 and 500 values are the maximum accepted document shapes; empty `keys` yields an unchanged deep copy. An unknown `action` raises `ValueError` in `api.dispatch`; the CLI prints the error message to stderr, writes nothing to stdout, and exits with status 2 (no traceback).
